## Iteration 2 — 2026-10-04 16:02:02
Item **01 Skeleton and test harness**: SOLVED.

### Completed
- **Tests first, and they failed 

Item 01 (skeleton and test harness) is done and marked `[x]`. The gate passes: all 1439 tests pass with no warnings, and `racket/` is unchanged. Nothing is committed; the driver will commit and push.

**What was built**
- **`python/metacat/qt/`**: `python3 -m metacat.qt` opens an empty window titled "Metacat" (1366×768). `--quit-after MS` makes it close by itself, for tests. `grab_png(widget, path)` saves a screenshot to a PNG. I looked at the grab of the empty window and it looks right. Importing the package doesn't need PySide6.
- **Test setup**: `pyproject.toml` has the `qt` extra and lists the `metacat.qt` package. `conftest.py` has a session `qapp` fixture that always runs offscreen and quits at the end, and a `grab` fixture. `run-tests.sh` keeps Qt offscreen and has a new `--qt` flag. Qt tests run in the normal fast and slow tiers.
- **Skipping without PySide6**: every `test_qt_*.py` starts with `pytest.importorskip("PySide6...")`. One test runs a fresh pytest with PySide6 hidden and checks that every Qt file is skipped.
- **Canvas command list**: `python/tests/data/tk-canvas-commands.json`, built by `tests/tk_canvas_inventory.py` from three sources: a scan of every place the code sends a canvas command, the two `sgl-tcl` fixture streams, and recording canvases in run 7 plus a justify run (120,344 commands). It has 14 commands:
  - creating rectangles, lines, ovals, arcs, polygons and text, each with its options;
  - `delete`, `move`, `itemconfigure` (with `-state` and `-tags`) and `bbox`;
  - `raise` and `scale`, which appear only in the fixtures, never in a run;
  - `canvasx` and `canvasy`, used only by the mouse handlers.

  It also lists the allowed values of some options (such as `-anchor`), what each command targets (an item id, `all` or a tag), the tag names (always single words) and the canvas methods. A test fails if any module sends something missing from the list, and also if a command name is computed rather than written out (apart from three known pass-through functions). A summary table is now in `docs/qt-gui-plan.md`.

**Two test-harness fixes, both logged in `docs/anomalies_and_quirks.md`**
- The pytest-qt plugin installed on this machine stops the whole pytest run when PySide6 can't be imported. I turned it off with `-p no:pytest-qt` in the pytest options. The similar-looking `-p no:pytestqt` is accepted but has no effect.
- The offscreen `QApplication` starts an extra thread, and later test files fork. The first gate run printed 32 warnings that this can deadlock. `conftest.py` now runs the `test_qt_*.py` files last, and a test checks the order; the second gate run had no warnings.

**Item 00 is still marked `[!]`.** Its session lost its API connection while the gate was running, but its files had already been committed, and their tests pass in this gate. I noted this in PROGRESS.md and didn't change the item; you or a later session can check it and mark it `[x]`.

